From 089d290da0a898503bdd8242f1172aef00c57612 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saverio Moscardini <4923627+savemosca@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:26:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MP2K shadow: read the driver's channels at its real tick

Mp2kShadow::frame_hook() is meant to run once per driver tick, at the
mixer's entry (SoundMainRAM): SoundInfo is then marked in flight
('Smsh'+1), the sequencer has updated the channels, and note-on flags
are not yet consumed by the mixer. That is how JRickey/gba-recomp calls
it, and why init() records the SoundMainRAM entries as hook keys.

The port never used those keys. GbaAudio polled frame_hook() every
sample_rate()/60 grid samples instead (1092 at 65536 Hz, against about
1097 per 59.73 Hz frame), so the poll drifted across the frame:
- Most polls found SoundInfo idle and returned as stale ticks, leaving
  gains and pitches frozen.
- Polls that did land inside a tick could fall after the mixer had
  consumed a note's START flag, so the note was missed.
The verifier then rejected the shadow or reverted it, and the player
heard the canon mix for much of the time.

The ARM runtime now has a read-only observer for a few exact dispatch
entries. The runtime registers the detected SoundMainRAM entries, and
calls GbaAudio::shadow_driver_tick() when guest code dispatches to one
of them; the fixed-rate poll is removed. Guest execution is unchanged:
the observer only reads memory, and nothing is installed for a ROM
without MP2K.

A summary line is logged when the session is suspended or ends:

  [audio] MP2K shadow (exit): live 97.0% of 600.0 s, driver ticks
    35830 (stale 0), reverts 1, unsupported waves 0

The engine did not log when the shadow substitutes, so the time it was
actually live could not be measured before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
